    dcterms:description "A course on Solid for people who want to build apps with it: why Solid exists, the linked data and RDF it is built on, vocabularies, pods and containers, reading and writing resources, identity and login, access control and sharing, notifications, designing an app's data, building, securing and publishing an app, a minimal app and Solid Memo itself read piece by piece, Solid's open problems, and the Linked Web Storage drafts that may succeed it. 17 chapters of short steps, each a piece of theory, with code and tables where they help, followed by multiple-choice questions; each chapter ends with a review, and every question you answer becomes a card in your deck. The facts come from the Solid specifications, the W3C standards around RDF, the servers' and libraries' documentation and code, and requests recorded on Community Solid Server 7.2, as of October 2026."@en ,
